  "bunch_spacing_limitation_note": "In Lu et al. (PRL 122, 014801, lines 143, 153-154, 255-257, 329-331; Lu thesis lines 2337-2341, 2365), the two bunches are spaced around one 1.3 GHz (PRL line 143) linac period T_b = 769.23 ps and fine-tuned in phase with laser splitters before the photocathode gun (PRL lines 153-154, 256-257, 329-331; thesis lines 2338-2341): an exact 1/(1.3 GHz, PRL line 143) spacing equals m = T_b * f_s = 8.785 cycles (282.5 deg mod 360 deg at 11.42 GHz, PRL lines 137, 149; 8.547 cycles, 196.9 deg mod 360 deg at the model f_pk = 11.1110 GHz) and is not in phase without optical delay tuning; instead, Lu's thesis (lines 2340-2341, 2365) states that 11.42 GHz is the 9th harmonic of a f_s/9 = 1.27 GHz bunch train with tuned spacing T_b = 9/f_s = 0.79 ns (788.09 ps; model 9/f_pk = 0.81 ns at f_pk/9 = 1.23 GHz). That ~0.79 ns (769.23 ps nominal) delay overlaps inside the 8 cm (N = 40) structure because t_p(N=40) = 1.96 ns > T_b, whereas in the short N = 8 model t_p(N=8) = 0.39 ns (0.598 ns at 20% threshold) < T_b = 769.23 ps, so two bunches at 769.23 ps spacing do not overlap in N = 8. The 86.36 MW curve is therefore a charge-scaled single-bunch estimate shifted by one synchronous RF period (Delta_t = 1/f_s = 90.00 ps).",
